<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  tingra-app.entitlements
  tingra-app

  Created by Larry Aasen on 2026-08-01.
  Copyright © 2026 Larry Aasen.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

  Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which denies camera and
  microphone access unless the binary opts in — hence the two device
  entitlements. disable-library-validation lets the host load a camera's
  CMIOExtension DAL plug-in, and third-party plug-ins generally, signed by
  a different team than this app (without it, CMIOGraphStart fails and no
  camera ever streams; the same fix appears in
  apps/tingra-cli/tingra-cli.entitlements and
  apps/tingra-cameras/tingra-cameras/tingra-cameras.entitlements). No
  sandbox entitlement: Tingra is deliberately unsandboxed. Screen Recording
  needs no entitlement — it is TCC-only.

  There is deliberately no keychain-access-groups entry. One was added for the
  destination store's shared keychain group, and it is gone for two reasons
  that arrived together (DESTINATIONS.md, "Key sharing between the app and the
  daemon"): tingra-cli cannot carry the entitlement at all — it is restricted,
  the kernel authorizes it from an embedded provisioning profile, and a bare
  Mach-O has nowhere to put one, which is what made v0.1.1 unrunnable — so
  there is no second party left to share a group with; and on this side it
  never took effect anyway, because automatic signing has only a wildcard App
  ID, whose profile cannot carry a keychain group. Xcode's response is not
  uniform: it silently dropped the entitlement from the signature in one
  configuration and failed the build outright in another, so a built app that
  launched was never evidence the group was working. Restoring it means
  provisioning Keychain Sharing on an explicit App ID, and that should follow
  the reopened key-sharing decision rather than precede it.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
